From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 15:44:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: G16: Count and elide redundant firmware dependency
 items (dep_elide)

Default-mode one-command Works carry up to two items (render: both
barrier-0 stages; compute: its own render lanes). They count against
queue_cap and the firmware's per-lane window. debugfs asahi_m4/dep_stats
counts items by redundancy class; dep_elide (bitmask, default 0,
runtime-writable) drops them: 1 an item on the same lane's earlier Work,
2 an item whose stamp is already reached at publish, 4 an item this
lane's previous Work already waited on (same stamp, equal or later).
Bits 1 and 4 assume in-order start within a lane and need a correctness
gate before any default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
